{
  "name": "Qualify inbound leads by their company domain with Alion",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Qualify inbound leads by company\n\n### How it works\nA visitor fills in the lead form. The workflow takes the domain of their work email (or of the website they typed) and asks Alion, a live graph of companies, which company it is. For a known company it then checks whether the company shows signs of life (open job postings, a site that answers, recent updates) and how many roles it is hiring for. Each lead is saved to an n8n Data Table with the company's name, industry, size, country and founding year, an Alion verdict and a status:\n- **qualified**: a known, active company larger than your minimum size;\n- **review**: a personal email address, a company Alion does not know, or one below your rules.\n\nIf Alion does not answer within two minutes, the lead is saved with **review** and a note to check it by hand, so no lead is lost. The visitor sees a thank-you page either way. Alion is called through its free open MCP address: no account or API key. The free allowance is 300 calls a day per network.\n\n### Setup\n1. In **Lead rules**, set the minimum company sizes you accept and the Data Table name (the table is created on the first submission).\n2. Activate the workflow and open the production URL of **Lead form**, or embed it on your site.\n3. Submit three test leads: a personal address, an address at a well-known company, and one at a made-up domain. Check the three rows in the Data Table.\n\n### Customization\nAdd a Slack or email node after **Save the lead** to alert sales about qualified leads, or send them to your CRM. Extend **Lead rules** with industries or countries you want to prioritise.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "c2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -700,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
